cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Greek Poverty Paradox"
abstract: >-
  A data-driven investigation into why Greek households report the EU's
  highest subjective financial strain — a 52.6-point gap, averaged over
  2015-2024, between the share reporting difficulty making ends meet
  (highest of 27 EU member states) and the official income-poverty rate,
  AROP (7th of 27) — and how much of that gap the available evidence can
  actually account for.
authors:
  - given-names: Stelios
